<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:32:default:default">
<!--
    kuna analysis (relocrebase, always on), GH-904: a big-endian
    relocatable object's analysis facts at the addresses the loader gives it.

    The analysis tier reads a relocatable object through a copy patched to the
    loader's layout, so every pass's addresses are load addresses.  The
    patcher wrote little-endian fields only and handed a big-endian object
    over unrebased, so its passes saw the pre-link addresses: the MIPS t9
    seed of a PIC function landed at its section offset, greet's prologue
    (lui gp,%hi(_gp_disp); addiu; addu gp,gp,t9) never resolved $gp, and its
    call through the GOT stayed a load from an unknown t9:
        (**(void (**)(int))(v1 + 0x98))(*(int *)(v1 + 0x9c) + 0x80);   (bug)
    and functions listed scale and greet twice, at 0x0 and 0x8 as well.
    The fields are now written in the object's own byte order.

    Stage: P1 program prep (relocatable layout).
    Single pass.

    Image: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/relocrebase_be_mips.o
    (relocrebase_be.c); see relocrebase_be.provenance.

    Assert #1: greet calls puts with its string.
    Assert #2: no t9 variable is left.
    Assert #3: each function is listed once, at its load address.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">03e0000800000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/relocrebase_be_mips.o</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>lo fu greet</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="relocrebase-be #1: greet calls puts with its string" min="1" max="1">puts\("hello from a big-endian object"\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="relocrebase-be #2: no t9 variable" min="0" max="0">// t9</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="relocrebase-be #3: greet is listed once, at its load address" min="1" max="1">^0x400008 greet</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="relocrebase-be #3b: nothing at a pre-link address" min="0" max="0">^0x[0-9a-f]{1,3} (scale|greet)</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
